IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg2-support`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1: section 141(d) to (i) and (k) -- CLASSES OF DIRECTORS, RELIANCE ON RECORDS AND
-- REPORTS, ACTION WITHOUT A MEETING, MEETINGS OUTSIDE THE STATE, COMPENSATION, PARTICIPATION BY TELEPHONE, AND REMOVAL.
--
-- SEAT: a director (protected, removable, consenting), a stockholder (voting to remove), an incorporator. The text is
-- de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt (a plain-text rendering, not the official text). Cross-reference taken as an input: section 116
-- (piece dg1), how a consent is documented, signed and delivered; "electronic transmission" is defined in section 232(d)(1) (piece dg5).
-- Dates "N year(s) thereafter" are counted with the core's calendar arithmetic (29 February plus 1 year is 28 February: core Fork F2).

§ `Section 141(d): classes of directors, and unequal votes`

DECLARE `s 141(d) Instrument that classifies the board` IS ONE OF
    `the certificate of incorporation, under s 141(d)`
    `an initial bylaw, under s 141(d)`
    `a bylaw adopted by a vote of the stockholders, under s 141(d)`
    `a bylaw adopted by the directors alone, under s 141(d)`

-- "The directors of any corporation organized under this chapter may, by the certificate of incorporation or by an initial bylaw,
-- or by a bylaw adopted by a vote of the stockholders, be divided into 1, 2 or 3 classes". A bylaw adopted by the directors alone
-- is none of the three the text names.
-- src:369 | The directors of any corporation organized under this chapter may, by the certificate of incorporation or by an initial bylaw, or by a bylaw adopted by a vote of the stockholders, be divided into 1, 2 or 3 classes; …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(d) (src:369)
GIVEN `the instrument` IS A `s 141(d) Instrument that classifies the board`
      `the number of classes` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 141(d) the directors may be divided into classes by the instrument` `the instrument` `the number of classes` MEANS
        (CONSIDER `the instrument`
         WHEN `the certificate of incorporation, under s 141(d)` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `an initial bylaw, under s 141(d)` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a bylaw adopted by a vote of the stockholders, under s 141(d)` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a bylaw adopted by the directors alone, under s 141(d)` THEN FALSE)
    AND (   `the number of classes` EQUALS 1
         OR `the number of classes` EQUALS 2
         OR `the number of classes` EQUALS 3)

-- "the term of office of those of the first class to expire at the first annual meeting held after such classification becomes
-- effective; of the second class 1 year thereafter; of the third class 2 years thereafter". A class other than 1, 2 or 3: not covered.
-- src:369 | the term of office of those of the first class to expire at the first annual meeting held after such classification becomes effective; of the second class 1 year thereafter; of the third class 2 years thereafter; …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(d) (src:369)
GIVEN `the class` IS A NUMBER
      `the date of the first annual meeting held after the classification becomes effective` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 141(d) the date the term of the class expires` `the class` `the date of the first annual meeting held after the classification becomes effective` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the class` EQUALS 1 THEN JUST `the date of the first annual meeting held after the classification becomes effective`
        IF `the class` EQUALS 2 THEN JUST (`the date` (`period in years` 1) `after` `the date of the first annual meeting held after the classification becomes effective`)
        IF `the class` EQUALS 3 THEN JUST (`the date` (`period in years` 2) `after` `the date of the first annual meeting held after the classification becomes effective`)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- "The certificate of incorporation or bylaw provision dividing the directors into classes may authorize the board of directors
-- to assign members of the board already in office to such classes at the time such classification becomes effective."
-- Without that authority the text does not say whether the board may assign them: NOTHING.
-- src:369 | The certificate of incorporation or bylaw provision dividing the directors into classes may authorize the board of directors to assign members of the board already in office to such classes at the time such classification becomes effective. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(d) (src:369)
GIVEN `the provision dividing the directors into classes authorizes the board to assign them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 141(d) the board may assign the directors in office to the classes` `the provision dividing the directors into classes authorizes the board to assign them` MEANS
    IF   `the provision dividing the directors into classes authorizes the board to assign them`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- "The certificate of incorporation may confer upon holders of any class or series of stock the right to elect 1 or more directors
-- who shall serve for such term, and have such voting powers as shall be stated in the certificate of incorporation."
-- Only the certificate confers this right.
-- src:369 | The certificate of incorporation may confer upon holders of any class or series of stock the right to elect 1 or more directors who shall serve for such term, and have such voting powers as shall be stated in the certificate of incorporation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(d) (src:369)
GIVEN `where the right is conferred` IS A `Where a provision is made`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 141(d) the holders of a class or series of stock may be given the right to elect directors` `where the right is conferred` MEANS
    `where the right is conferred` EQUALS `in the certificate of incorporation`

-- "The terms of office and voting powers of the directors elected separately by the holders of any class or series of stock may be
-- greater than or less than those of any other director or class of directors. In addition, the certificate of incorporation may confer
-- upon 1 or more directors, whether or not elected separately by the holders of any class or series of stock, voting powers
-- greater than or less than those of other directors." Only the certificate confers voting powers on a director, other than as
-- the classified election provides.
-- src:369 | In addition, the certificate of incorporation may confer upon 1 or more directors, whether or not elected separately by the holders of any class or series of stock, voting powers greater than or less than those of other directors. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(d) (src:369)
GIVEN `where the greater or lesser voting power is conferred` IS A `Where a provision is made`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 141(d) a director may be given greater or lesser voting power than other directors` `where the greater or lesser voting power is conferred` MEANS
    `where the greater or lesser voting power is conferred` EQUALS `in the certificate of incorporation`

-- "Any such provision conferring greater or lesser voting power shall apply to voting in any committee, unless otherwise provided in
-- the certificate of incorporation or bylaws."
-- src:369 | Any such provision conferring greater or lesser voting power shall apply to voting in any committee, unless otherwise provided in the certificate of incorporation or bylaws. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(d) (src:369)
GIVEN `where it is otherwise provided` IS A `Where a provision is made`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 141(d) the greater or lesser voting power applies to voting in a committee` `where it is otherwise provided` MEANS
    NOT (`dg2 the place is the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws` `where it is otherwise provided`)

-- "If the certificate of incorporation provides that 1 or more directors shall have more or less than 1 vote per director on any
-- matter, every reference in this chapter to a majority or other proportion of the directors shall refer to a majority or other
-- proportion of the votes of the directors." TRUE: the references count the votes of the directors, not the directors.
-- src:369 | If the certificate of incorporation provides that 1 or more directors shall have more or less than 1 vote per director on any matter, every reference in this chapter to a majority or other proportion of the directors shall refer to a majority or other proportion of the votes of the directors.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(d) (src:369)
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation gives 1 or more directors more or less than 1 vote per director on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 141(d) a majority or other proportion of the directors is a proportion of the votes of the directors` `the certificate of incorporation gives 1 or more directors more or less than 1 vote per director on the matter` MEANS
    `the certificate of incorporation gives 1 or more directors more or less than 1 vote per director on the matter`

§ `Section 141(e): reliance on records and reports`

DECLARE `s 141(e) What the member relied on` IS ONE OF
    `the records of the corporation`
    `information, opinions, reports or statements presented to the corporation by an officer or employee of the corporation`
    `information, opinions, reports or statements presented to the corporation by a committee of the board of directors`
    `information, opinions, reports or statements presented to the corporation by any other person`

-- "A member of the board of directors, or a member of any committee designated by the board of directors, shall, in the performance
-- of such member's duties, be fully protected in relying in good faith upon the records of the corporation and upon such
-- information, opinions, reports or statements presented to the corporation by any of the corporation's officers or employees, or
-- committees of the board of directors, or by any other person as to matters the member reasonably believes are within such other
-- person's professional or expert competence and who has been selected with reasonable care by or on behalf of the corporation."
-- Fork F-141-5: the qualification "as to matters the member reasonably believes are within such other person's professional or
-- expert competence and who has been selected with reasonable care" is read as attaching to "any other person" alone.
-- src:370 | A member of the board of directors, or a member of any committee designated by the board of directors, shall, in the performance of such member’s duties, be fully protected in relying in good faith upon the records of the corporation and upon such information, opinions, reports or statements presented to the corporation by any of the corporation’s officers or employees, or committees of the board of directors, or by any other person as to matters the member reasonably believes are within such other person’s professional or expert competence and who has been selected with reasonable care by or on behalf of the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(e) (src:370)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the board of directors or of a committee designated by it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person relied in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what was relied on` IS A `s 141(e) What the member relied on`
      `the member reasonably believes the matter is within the other person's professional or expert competence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person was selected with reasonable care by or on behalf of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 141(e) the member is fully protected in relying` `the person is a member of the board of directors or of a committee designated by it` `the person relied in good faith` `what was relied on` `the member reasonably believes the matter is within the other person's professional or expert competence` `the other person was selected with reasonable care by or on behalf of the corporation` MEANS
        `the person is a member of the board of directors or of a committee designated by it`
    AND `the person relied in good faith`
    AND (CONSIDER `what was relied on`
         WHEN `the records of the corporation` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `information, opinions, reports or statements presented to the corporation by an officer or employee of the corporation` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `information, opinions, reports or statements presented to the corporation by a committee of the board of directors` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `information, opinions, reports or statements presented to the corporation by any other person` THEN
                 `the member reasonably believes the matter is within the other person's professional or expert competence`
             AND `the other person was selected with reasonable care by or on behalf of the corporation`)

§ `Section 141(f): action without a meeting`

-- "any action required or permitted to be taken at any meeting of the board of directors or of any committee thereof may be taken
-- without a meeting if all members of the board or committee, as the case may be, consent thereto in writing, or by electronic
-- transmission, and (2) a consent may be documented, signed and delivered in any manner permitted by section 116", "Unless
-- otherwise restricted by the certificate of incorporation or bylaws".
-- out of range: section 116 (piece dg1): whether the consents are documented, signed and delivered as it allows is a plain input.
-- out of range: section 232(d)(1) (piece dg5): "electronic transmission" is defined there; whether a consent is one is a plain fact here.
-- src:371 | Unless otherwise restricted by the certificate of incorporation or bylaws, (1) any action required or permitted to be taken at any meeting of the board of directors or of any committee thereof may be taken without a meeting if all members of the board or committee, as the case may be, consent thereto in writing, or by electronic transmission, and (2) a consent may be documented, signed and delivered in any manner permitted by § 116 of this title. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(f) (src:371)
GIVEN `the number of members of the board or committee` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of members who consent in writing or by electronic transmission` IS A NUMBER
      `the consents are documented, signed and delivered in a manner permitted by section 116` IS A BOOLEAN
      `where the restriction is made` IS A `Where a provision is made`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 141(f) the board or committee may act without a meeting` `the number of members of the board or committee` `the number of members who consent in writing or by electronic transmission` `the consents are documented, signed and delivered in a manner permitted by section 116` `where the restriction is made` MEANS
        (`the number of members of the board or committee` AT LEAST 1)
    AND (`the number of members who consent in writing or by electronic transmission` EQUALS `the number of members of the board or committee`)
    AND `the consents are documented, signed and delivered in a manner permitted by section 116`
    AND NOT (`dg2 the place is the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws` `where the restriction is made`)

-- "Any person (whether or not then a director) may provide, whether through instruction to an agent or otherwise, that a consent to
-- action will be effective at a future time (including a time determined upon the happening of an event), no later than 60 days
-- after such instruction is given or such provision is made and such consent shall be deemed to have been given for purposes of this
-- subsection at such effective time so long as such person is then a director and did not revoke the consent prior to such time."
-- The last day is inside the 60 days (core Fork F3).
-- src:371 | Any person (whether or not then a director) may provide, whether through instruction to an agent or otherwise, that a consent to action will be effective at a future time (including a time determined upon the happening of an event), no later than 60 days after such instruction is given or such provision is made and such consent shall be deemed to have been given for purposes of this subsection at such effective time so long as such person is then a director and did not revoke the consent prior to such time. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(f) (src:371)
GIVEN `the date the instruction is given or the provision is made` IS A DATE
      `the date the consent is to be effective` IS A DATE
      `the person is a director at that time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person revoked the consent before that time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 141(f) the consent is deemed given at its effective time` `the date the instruction is given or the provision is made` `the date the consent is to be effective` `the person is a director at that time` `the person revoked the consent before that time` MEANS
        (`the date the consent is to be effective` AT MOST (`the date` (`period in days` 60) `after` `the date the instruction is given or the provision is made`))
    AND `the person is a director at that time`
    AND NOT `the person revoked the consent before that time`

-- "Any such consent shall be revocable prior to its becoming effective." After it is effective the text does not say.
-- src:371 | Any such consent shall be revocable prior to its becoming effective. After an action is taken, the consent or consents relating thereto shall be filed with the minutes of the proceedings of the board of directors, or the committee thereof, in the same paper or electronic form as the minutes are maintained.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(f) (src:371)
GIVEN `the consent has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 141(f) the consent may be revoked` `the consent has become effective` MEANS
    IF   `the consent has become effective`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- "After an action is taken, the consent or consents relating thereto shall be filed with the minutes of the proceedings of the board
-- of directors, or the committee thereof, in the same paper or electronic form as the minutes are maintained."
-- src:371 | After an action is taken, the consent or consents relating thereto shall be filed with the minutes of the proceedings of the board of directors, or the committee thereof, in the same paper or electronic form as the minutes are maintained.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(f) (src:371)
GIVEN `the consents are filed with the minutes of the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consents are filed in the same paper or electronic form as the minutes are maintained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 141(f) the consents have been filed as the Law requires` `the consents are filed with the minutes of the proceedings` `the consents are filed in the same paper or electronic form as the minutes are maintained` MEANS
        `the consents are filed with the minutes of the proceedings`
    AND `the consents are filed in the same paper or electronic form as the minutes are maintained`

§ `Section 141(g), (h) and (i): meetings, compensation, participation by telephone`

-- src:372 | Unless otherwise restricted by the certificate of incorporation or bylaws, the board of directors of any corporation organized under this chapter may hold its meetings, and have an office or offices, outside of this State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(g) (src:372)
GIVEN `where the restriction is made` IS A `Where a provision is made`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 141(g) the board may hold its meetings, and have an office or offices, outside this State` `where the restriction is made` MEANS
    NOT (`dg2 the place is the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws` `where the restriction is made`)

-- src:373 | Unless otherwise restricted by the certificate of incorporation or bylaws, the board of directors shall have the authority to fix the compensation of directors.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(h) (src:373)
GIVEN `where the restriction is made` IS A `Where a provision is made`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 141(h) the board has the authority to fix the compensation of directors` `where the restriction is made` MEANS
    NOT (`dg2 the place is the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws` `where the restriction is made`)

-- "members of the board of directors of any corporation, or any committee designated by the board, may participate in a meeting of
-- such board, or committee by means of conference telephone or other communications equipment by means of which all persons
-- participating in the meeting can hear each other, and participation in a meeting pursuant to this subsection shall constitute
-- presence in person at the meeting."
-- src:374 | Unless otherwise restricted by the certificate of incorporation or bylaws, members of the board of directors of any corporation, or any committee designated by the board, may participate in a meeting of such board, or committee by means of conference telephone or other communications equipment by means of which all persons participating in the meeting can hear each other, and participation in a meeting pursuant to this subsection shall constitute presence in person at the meeting.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(i) (src:374)
GIVEN `the member participates by conference telephone or other communications equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all persons participating in the meeting can hear each other` IS A BOOLEAN
      `where the restriction is made` IS A `Where a provision is made`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 141(i) the participation constitutes presence in person at the meeting` `the member participates by conference telephone or other communications equipment` `all persons participating in the meeting can hear each other` `where the restriction is made` MEANS
        `the member participates by conference telephone or other communications equipment`
    AND `all persons participating in the meeting can hear each other`
    AND NOT (`dg2 the place is the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws` `where the restriction is made`)

§ `Section 141(k): removal of directors`

DECLARE `s 141(k) Removal` HAS
    `the removal is for cause` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the board is classified as provided in subsection (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate of incorporation provides that stockholders may remove a classified board without cause` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the corporation has cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN
    `less than the entire board is to be removed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the votes cast against the removal would be sufficient to elect the director if then cumulatively voted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the director was elected by the holders of a class or series of stock under the certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of shares then entitled to vote at an election of directors` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of those shares voted in favor of removal` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of shares of the class or series then entitled to vote` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of those shares voted in favor of removal, of the class or series` IS A NUMBER

GIVETH A `Vote base`
`s 141(k) the shares then entitled to vote at an election of directors as a vote base` MEANS
    `another base named in the provision` "the shares then entitled to vote at an election of directors"

GIVETH A `Vote base`
`s 141(k) the outstanding shares of the class or series as a vote base` MEANS
    `another base named in the provision` "the outstanding shares of that class or series"

-- "Any director or the entire board of directors may be removed, with or without cause, by the holders of a majority of the shares
-- then entitled to vote at an election of directors, except as follows: (1) Unless the certificate of incorporation otherwise
-- provides, in the case of a corporation whose board is classified as provided in subsection (d) of this section, stockholders
-- may effect such removal only for cause; or (2) In the case of a corporation having cumulative voting, if less than the entire
-- board is to be removed, no director may be removed without cause if the votes cast against such director's removal would be
-- sufficient to elect such director if then cumulatively voted at an election of the entire board of directors, or, if there be
-- classes of directors, at an election of the class of directors of which such director is a part." The last paragraph: for the removal
-- without cause of a director elected by the holders of a class or series, the vote is that of the outstanding shares of that class
-- or series and not of the outstanding shares as a whole. Fork F-141-6: the text names the class vote only for removal without cause;
-- for removal for cause the whole vote is taken.
-- src:376 | Any director or the entire board of directors may be removed, with or without cause, by the holders of a majority of the shares then entitled to vote at an election of directors, except as follows:
-- src:377 | Unless the certificate of incorporation otherwise provides, in the case of a corporation whose board is classified as provided in subsection (d) of this section, stockholders may effect such removal only for cause; or
-- src:378 | In the case of a corporation having cumulative voting, if less than the entire board is to be removed, no director may be removed without cause if the votes cast against such director’s removal would be sufficient to elect such director if then cumulatively voted at an election of the entire board of directors, or, if there be classes of directors, at an election of the class of directors of which such director is a part.
-- src:379 | Whenever the holders of any class or series are entitled to elect 1 or more directors by the certificate of incorporation, this subsection shall apply, in respect to the removal without cause of a director or directors so elected, to the vote of the holders of the outstanding shares of that class or series and not to the vote of the outstanding shares as a whole.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(k) (src:376-379)
GIVEN r IS A `s 141(k) Removal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 141(k) the stockholders may remove the director` r MEANS
    `dg2 both findings hold`
        (IF   r's `the director was elected by the holders of a class or series of stock under the certificate of incorporation` AND (NOT r's `the removal is for cause`)
         THEN `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `s 141(k) the outstanding shares of the class or series as a vote base`)
                  (r's `the number of those shares voted in favor of removal, of the class or series`)
                  (r's `the number of shares of the class or series then entitled to vote`)
         ELSE `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `s 141(k) the shares then entitled to vote at an election of directors as a vote base`)
                  (r's `the number of those shares voted in favor of removal`)
                  (r's `the number of shares then entitled to vote at an election of directors`))
        (JUST (   r's `the removal is for cause`
              OR NOT (   (r's `the board is classified as provided in subsection (d)` AND (NOT r's `the certificate of incorporation provides that stockholders may remove a classified board without cause`))
                      OR (   r's `the corporation has cumulative voting`
                         AND r's `less than the entire board is to be removed`
                         AND r's `the votes cast against the removal would be sufficient to elect the director if then cumulatively voted`))))
